+### Stage 0 exit criteria
+
+Stage 0 establishes a decision-ready preparation and feasibility baseline.
+Its closure package must contain:
+
+1. Exact repository revisions, local-change inventories, source authority and
+   documented source/document conflicts for the three required components.
+2. A pinned host/tool baseline and reproducible commands for the minimum
+   observed build/virtual experiments, including failures and limitations.
+3. Observed versus proposed component responsibilities, dependency directions,
+   trust/admission boundaries and a justified candidate integrated scenario.
+4. A known-defect/uncertainty ledger with evidence, owners, consequences,
+   bounded next actions and separate adoption gates.
+5. Four separate board records with provenance, possession status, unknowns
+   and explicit feasibility status. Unavailable hardware remains BLOCKED.
+6. Locally recoverable evidence, input identities and reproduction recipes,
+   with missing provenance and backup limitations disclosed.
+7. An exit checklist identifying closure blockers versus accepted/deferred
+   engineering risks, and a concrete reviewable next-stage/engineering scope.
+
+Closing Stage 0 does not require fixing every defect, booting Linux/vGIC,
+completing integration, acquiring boards, physical validation or evaluation.
+Blocked physical work and bounded engineering risks may be carried forward
+explicitly. Closure and a stage transition require an explicit review decision;
+a closure recommendation alone does not change the current stage.
+
+### Thesis stages versus implementation milestones
+
+The thesis stages below are research and evidence decision gates.
+M0–M5 in the linked implementation roadmap are engineering work packages that
+can span those stages. They are not additional Stage 0 exit requirements.
+In particular M1 Linux/vGIC, M3 integration, M4 physical validation and M5
+evaluation are later delivery work. Completing M0 is not required for Stage 0
+closure either: its identified risks and next correction must be reviewable.
+Stage 1 formulates and approves the research question/architecture before
+dependent features; separately approved small baseline bugfixes retain their
+own scope. Neither milestone completion nor a Stage 0 closure decision grants
+blanket approval for the rest of the roadmap.
+
 | Stage                      | Owner and required work                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | Exit evidence / decision                                                                                                                                                                                 |
