+## Stage 0 closure review proposal (2026-10-25)
+
+**Status remains in progress; no transition declared.** The
+[closure package](../haven/docs/methodology/stage0/20261025-closure/README.md)
+recommends closing preparation with recorded risks, subject to explicit review.
+Its exit checklist distinguishes missing preparation evidence from later
+engineering/hardware delivery. M0–M5 are implementation work packages spanning
+thesis stages; M1 Linux/vGIC, M3 integration, M4 physical validation, M5
+evaluation and completion of M0 do not gate Stage0 closure. Earlier “Stage0
+work remaining” wording is historical backlog rather than new exit criteria.
+
+No audits or mechanism experiments were restarted. The existing register,
+fault/disassembly and strict/default evidence was reviewed against Arm's
+memory-model rules and GCC15.2 documentation. For the captured traditional
+EL2 regime, stage-1-disabled Device data accesses explain the unaligned faults
+despite A=0. The recommended next A1 contract is a restricted strict-access
+bootstrap ending before external table publication, secondary release, guest
+execution or unreviewed sharing;
+it is not an implemented profile. Normal-memory translation/cache setup is a
+separate possible extension. The existing spinlock exclusive helpers have
+definitions but no caller in the inspected implementation; strict compilation
+does not certify them or SMP/cache-alias semantics.
+
+A2's existing build/symbol/native/ARM64 evidence supports recommending its
+unchanged nine-line memcpy patch for independent adoption review, with final-
+tree focused checks and the separate A1 risk recorded. No patch is applied.
+Coordinated CP1 schema/CLI implementation is recommended deferred: current
+inventories/manual recipes already retire the immediate wrong-input/failure-
+ownership risk, while runtime consumers/architecture remain unsettled.
+
+The next concrete engineering proposal is HAVEN-only EP-A2; Stage1 research
+question/threat-model/architecture formulation is a separate next thesis
+decision. All three repositories remain required. Effort ranges, dependencies
+and hardware assumptions are in the closure backlog. Four physical targets
+remain BLOCKED; local-only backup/provenance limitations remain recorded risks.
+Explicit closure/adoption decisions are pending, not inferred from this review.
